                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that ingathers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6af9ca35-5815-4d76-a4f1-bf628f51a274",
                                "sense_id": "b0017e19-7c19-3687-a4f6-3253a53a86f3",
                                "text": "I think that Jesus is a gatherer in of human misery. It was to be such an ingatherer that he came on earth — that was his one object; to fit himself for that he became man at all, and lived, and died."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c85bd3cd-a08c-49cb-a3db-e1777809c718",
                                "sense_id": "b0017e19-7c19-3687-a4f6-3253a53a86f3",
                                "text": "The Wind in sooth is an ingatherer. When fire goes out, it sinks into the Wind. When the sun goes down, it sinks into the Wind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2046a54d-882b-4ca7-b1fc-111a339b8d28",
                                "sense_id": "b0017e19-7c19-3687-a4f6-3253a53a86f3",
                                "text": "Implicit in the notion of Israel as being the 'ingatherer of the exiles' is the idea that there is a larger political community beyond its borders."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
